        <p>Fellowes states this model provides an increased height adjustment range for taller users, up to 6.25" above the desktop. That is the closest thing to a tall-specific claim in this category, and unlike most such claims it maps to a published number rather than to adjectives.</p>

        <p>Run the arithmetic on it. A 29" desk plus 6.25" gives a 35.25" typing surface. That is well short of a 6'4" user's 43"–45" standing target, so this tray is not a substitute for a converter or a full standing desk. What it does well is bridge a partial sit-stand setup on a desk that is already somewhat raised, or provide the tilt-and-height correction alongside a desk you have already raised by other means.</p>

